femforge.elmer.sif follows the public API shape of pyelmer (GPL-3.0,
https://github.com/nemocrys/pyelmer); it is an independent implementation.
The golden files in tests/elmer/fixtures/sif_reference were written by pyelmer.

femforge imports gmsh (GPL-2.0-or-later, https://gmsh.info) at run time. gmsh is
installed separately from PyPI and is not part of this product; software that
combines femforge with gmsh is subject to gmsh's license.

femforge runs Elmer FEM (GPL-2.0-or-later; the ElmerSolver library is
LGPL-2.1-or-later; https://github.com/ElmerCSC/elmerfem) as a separate program.
The femforge-elmer container image redistributes Elmer and Ubuntu packages under
their own licenses. Their license texts are in /usr/share/elmersolver/license_texts
(Elmer) and /usr/share/doc (Ubuntu packages) inside the image;
https://docs.femforge.io/user-guide/elmer/#image-licenses lists their sources.

femforge-workbench bundles a JavaScript client built from packages under the
MIT, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Apache-2.0, Zlib and 0BSD licenses, and the Inter and
JetBrains Mono fonts under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
femforge_workbench/widgets/serve/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt and
femforge_workbench/widgets/serve/fonts/ hold their license texts and notices.

femforge-workbench resolves colormaps through colorcet, whose colormaps are
licensed under CC-BY-4.0: Peter Kovesi, "Good Colour Maps: How to Design Them",
arXiv:1509.03700 (2015), https://colorcet.holoviz.org.
